Products designed without wear-part separation become scrap when minor wear elements fail because refurbishment economics cannot justify wear-element restoration. Isolating wear concentrates degradation in economically replaceable modules, preserving durable cores across multiple refurbishment cycles. Wear-part isolation extends core lifespan and reduces total material throughput.

Clear wear-part identification enables faster refurbishment decision-making and reduces refurbishment complexity. Concentrated wear enables predictive replacement scheduling, improving refurbished product reliability. Modular wear parts enable user maintenance, extending product lifespan beyond formal refurbishment cycles.